ned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can factor the expression using the difference of squares formula with $a=x$ and $b=2$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^{2} - 4 &=  \\\\\nx^{2} - 2^{2} &=  \\\\\n&= (x + 2)(x - 2)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065342 #edb/ref 1065 1599 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065342 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "3f50b677-50fc-5584-82de-7ad393d19d72" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065342 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065375 #edb/ref 1064 "To multiply a binomial and a trinomial, we take each term of the binomial and multiply it by every term in the trinomial. Then, we simplify by collecting like terms.\n\nFor example, to multiply $({\\color{blue}{x}} + {\\color{red}{3}})$ and $(x^2 + 2x+4),$ we multiply ${\\color{blue}{x}}$ and $(x^2 + 2x+4),$ and then we add this to the product of ${\\color{red}{3}}$ and $(x^2 + 2x+4).$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+3)({x}^{2}+2x+4) & = \\\\ x({x}^{2}+2x+4)+3({x}^{2}+2x+4) & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+4x+3{x}^{2}+6x+12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we group the like terms and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+4x+3{x}^{2}+6x+12 & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+3{x}^{2}+4x+6x+12 & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+10x+12\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065375 #edb/ref 1065 4089 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065375 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "abdf5593-94a7-5f4c-a2ec-ca378d5b0034" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065375 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067720 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186498885 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067720 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186498914 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067720 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186498964 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067720 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186498991 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067720 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186499029 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067720 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186067720 #edb/